---
// Home (site-prelaunch.md §2, v2.3 — Ledger re-expression: product-proof hero +
// five new sections, human-approved concept study 2026-07-05, #417). Deep door
// leads the hero sub; "Or, take any US-listed ticker" demo turn follows above the fold
// (demo-retention guardrail). Copy slots pending Growth #63 (site-copy-twiceover.md
// reconciliation per ADR 0042 pivot) for the hero/how-it-works/what-its-not text —
// do not reword; layout must not change when #63 lands.
// The "Connect read-only →" CTA and header sign-in slot were reserved (ADR 0042/0074)
// until app-launch (#32); both are now built (#1754, site-app-seam.md §3/§4) as
// same-origin /go/* redirects — see Base.astro for the header slot. The entry-box row
// was built earlier, v2.6, fixture-only, no backend call (#1240, ADR 0383,
// site-prelaunch.md §2/§6, Designer artifact ai-team/design/assets/fixture-demo-open-door.html)
// — its live handoff (carrying the typed ticker) is a separate, still-gated build.
// v2.3 NEW SECTIONS (Depth strip, Two doors, Showcase band, Trust plate, FAQ):
// copy below is Engineer-drafted structural placeholder text — facts already
// established elsewhere (the constitution's own data/privacy rules, the NVDA
// fixture, existing Growth-approved wys copy folded into the two door cards) —
// pending the PM/Growth copy-slot pass before this ships past a preview deploy,
// same status as the rest of the page's placeholder text (site-prelaunch.md v2.3).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ProductProofVisual from "../components/ProductProofVisual.astro";
import AnalysisBand from "../components/AnalysisBand.astro";
import BeforeAfterRead from "../components/BeforeAfterRead.astro";
import MobileShowcase from "../components/MobileShowcase.astro";
import TechnicalsPriceChart from "../components/TechnicalsPriceChart.astro";

// Organization + WebSite JSON-LD (SEO audit 2026-07 finding 7) — brand-SERP/knowledge-panel
// groundwork. No FAQPage schema: Google deprecated FAQ rich results 2026-05-07.
// sameAs/logo (SEO re-audit 2026-08-23, stock-analyst-platform#2634): the X account didn't exist in
// July, does now — sameAs links the two brand surfaces for knowledge-panel eligibility and AI-answer
// entity resolution. logo points at the existing square PWA icon (already served, no new asset).
const organizationJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  name: "TwiceOver",
  url: "https://twiceover.io",
  email: "support@twiceover.io",
  sameAs: ["https://x.com/twiceover_io"],
  logo: "https://twiceover.io/icon-192.png",
};
const websiteJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebSite",
  name: "TwiceOver",
  url: "https://twiceover.io",
};
---
<Base
  title="TwiceOver — a second look at your own book"
  description="Connect your brokerage read-only and the read runs on the positions you actually hold — your rules, your horizons. Or take any US-listed ticker — no account, no connection needed. Depth, never a verdict."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(organizationJsonLd)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(websiteJsonLd)} />
  {/* Hero — deep door leads the sub (ADR 0042, connect-led); demo retained above the fold.
      No pricing link in the reserved-box state: pricing via header nav + foot Pricing cue. */}
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero__copy">
      <h1 class="type-display">A second look at your own book.</h1>
      <p class="sub">
        Connect your brokerage <strong>read-only</strong> and the read runs on the positions
        you actually hold — measured against <strong>your own rules</strong>, across near-, mid-,
        and far-term horizons. <strong>Depth, never a verdict.</strong>
      </p>
      {/* "Connect read-only →" quiet-outline CTA (#1754, ADR 0042/0074) — same-origin
          /go/connect redirect to the app's entry point. No interim OAuth plumbing
          here; the app owns the actual OAuth flow. */}
      <a class="btn-quiet hero__cta" href="/go/connect">Connect read-only →</a>
      {/* Caption RETIRED — ADR 0748 Amendment 3, site-prelaunch.md §2 v2.27
          (stock-analyst-platform#2852). It read "Part of Core. Starts with a 14-day free trial." and
          existed to name the plan and the trial standing between this press and the connector. The
          founder decision on epic stock-analyst-platform#2811 removed both from this road — a
          signed-up Free account may connect a brokerage read-only — so the line was not reworded but
          struck: there is nothing left to disclose before the press. The amendment is explicit that
          nothing replaces it; a new supporting line, if this page wants one, is Growth's call under
          stock-analyst-platform#2812. The CTA label above is untouched and stays locked
          (ADR 0042/0074). */}
      <p class="demo-turn">Or, take any US-listed ticker — no connection needed.</p>
      {/* The live ticker handoff (#2520, ADR 0383 Amendment 1, consult 0739) — replaces the
          v2.6 fixture-only demo. A plain HTML GET submit: the browser serializes `ticker` and
          navigates same-origin to /go/try, whose Worker bounds the value to /^[A-Z]{1,6}$/ and
          302s to the app. ("no JavaScript anywhere" struck — the typeahead below is JavaScript
          on this page; the SUBMIT is still a plain GET the browser performs, and the form works
          unchanged with the script absent.) Three attributes are pinned exactly and
          enforced by ci/check-entry-box.mjs — name="ticker", method="get", action="/go/try";
          `method` is never `post` (a body travels off-URL) and `action` is never external.
          The app prefills and focuses its own box but NEVER auto-submits: the second press is
          the assent act, covered by the app-side notice on direct/bare-URL app arrivals
          (ADR 0442 Amendment 1 R5) — this page no longer carries its own notice (ADR 0442
          Amendment 3, stock-analyst-platform#2960: founder call, site-side leg retired).
          CORRECTED (ADR 0810 build order item 6, stock-analyst-platform#2965): this page used to
          state "Deliberately absent: any script reading .value, and any fetch/XHR/WebSocket/
          sendBeacon on this page." Half of that is no longer true and the sentence does not
          survive the mechanism changing. What holds now:
            - a script DOES read this field's value, on every keystroke — the ticker/company-name
              typeahead (src/typeahead/, R1–R8 of read-components.md §6), signed off as a carve-out
              (ADR 0810) and reviewed by Security (consult 0811). It ships as a bundle under
              /_astro/, never inline: an inline script reading a field remains barred outright by
              ci/check-entry-box.mjs, and the Worker's script-src 'self' admits no inline exception.
            - the transmission ban is UNCHANGED and now enforced twice. No script on this page opens
              a connection of any kind; ci/check-entry-box.mjs scans every bundled body for the
              barred calls at build time, and the Worker's Content-Security-Policy `connect-src
              'none'` backstops it in the browser at runtime.
          The typeahead consults a committed, EDGAR-derived symbol index bundled with the site and
          nothing else — it never speaks to a server, and selecting a suggestion fills the field
          but NEVER submits (R6). The press below stays the one and only assent act. With the
          script absent or failed, this form is exactly the plain HTML GET it always was. */}
      <form class="entry-box" id="entry-form" action="/go/try" method="get" novalidate>
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="entry-ticker">A ticker</label>
        {/* The wrapper is what the listbox anchors to (position: relative in site.css), and it
            carries the input's flex sizing so the row's geometry is unchanged. */}
        <div class="symbol-combobox entry-box__field-wrap">
          <input id="entry-ticker" name="ticker" type="text" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="A ticker — NVDA" />
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="entry-box__submit">Get the read</button>
      </form>
    </div>
    <ProductProofVisual />
  </section>

  {/* Analysis band (v2.13, new, #2179) — the eight analysis sections, flowing
      continuously. Placed directly below the hero — the fixture-demo reveal it
      used to sit above retired v2.19; the live ticker handoff now sends that
      same visitor to a real read instead. */}
  <AnalysisBand />

  {/* Before/after read (v2.13, #2179 — build reference ai-team/design/assets/landing-
      carousel-hero-refresh-2026-08-14.html). Moved 5th -> 3rd, directly after the analysis
      band, per site-prelaunch.md v2.36 §2 (founder-directed 31 Aug, #3008). */}
  <BeforeAfterRead />

  {/* Depth strip (v2.3, new) — four structural facts about the product's construction,
      never a performance/returns claim (spec §2). */}
  <section class="depth-strip" aria-label="TwiceOver at a glance">
    <div class="container depth-strip__inner">
      <div class="depth-stat">
        <p class="depth-stat__figure type-display">8</p>
        <p class="depth-stat__caption">Analysis sections the engine draws on.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="depth-stat">
        <p class="depth-stat__figure type-display">4</p>
        <p class="depth-stat__caption">Paths for every structure you hold — including making no change. Full math, never a ranking.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="depth-stat">
        <p class="depth-stat__figure type-display">3</p>
        <p class="depth-stat__caption">Horizons in every outlook — near, mid, and far — each stated as a condition, never a verdict.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="depth-stat">
        <p class="depth-stat__figure type-display">Read-only</p>
        <p class="depth-stat__caption">TwiceOver can view your positions — it can never place, change, or cancel an order.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Two doors (v2.3, replaces "What you see") — two door cards, each ending in a
      static illustrative decoration, not a live control (spec §2). Checklist copy
      folds in the existing Growth-approved (#63) wys content, restructured. */}
  <section class="doors section-ground" aria-labelledby="two-doors">
    <h2 id="two-doors" class="type-heading-1 section-heading">Two doors</h2>
    <div class="door-grid">
      <article class="door">
        <p class="door__tag type-caption">The open door</p>
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">Any US-listed ticker, no connection needed</h3>
        <p class="door__body">Type any US-listed ticker — no connection needed — and get the same read, built from licensed data.</p>
        <ul class="door__checklist">
          <li><span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">›</span> The key technical levels, the macro backdrop and market regime, peer positioning, and fundamentals — each with its source and timestamp. Curated voices and the news wire are part of Core.</li>
          <li><span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">›</span> One conditional, multi-horizon outlook, each stated as a condition. Labeled AI synthesis; every figure from the data pipeline, not the model. Never a score, never a "buy" or "sell."</li>
          <li><span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">›</span> The same engine either way — connecting read-only changes what the read is measured against, not the read itself.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="door__decor door__decor--entry" role="presentation">
          <input type="text" value="A ticker — NVDA" disabled aria-hidden="true" />
          <span class="door__decor-btn" aria-hidden="true">Get the read</span>
        </div>
        <p class="door__decor-caption type-caption">Illustrative example — not a live control.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="door">
        <p class="door__tag type-caption">The deep door</p>
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">Connect read-only, see your own book</h3>
        <p class="door__body">Link your brokerage read-only and the same engine runs on the positions you actually hold.</p>
        <ul class="door__checklist">
          <li><span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">›</span> Your structure, with the math — your legs grouped into the position you actually hold, with net debit/credit, breakevens, max profit, max loss, and current P&amp;L.</li>
          <li><span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">›</span> Your rules, on live data — the profit targets, DTE thresholds, and max-loss lines you configured, evaluated against where the position is right now.</li>
          <li><span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">›</span> Your paths, with the full math — the moves available on what you hold, each with its complete numbers and trigger levels. No ranking, no "do this."</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="door__decor door__decor--positions" role="presentation">
          <div class="position-row"><span>NVDA</span><span>bull call spread</span><span>+$612</span></div>
          <div class="position-row"><span>MSFT</span><span>covered call</span><span>+$105</span></div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Mobile-app showcase (v2.13, part of the band that replaced the old three-artifact
      showcase, #2179 — build reference ai-team/design/assets/landing-carousel-
      hero-refresh-2026-08-14.html). Its own position in the DOM is unchanged by v2.36's
      reorder; it simply follows `doors` now that BeforeAfterRead sits at 3rd. */}
  <MobileShowcase />

  <section class="section-ground section-ground--recessed" aria-labelledby="how-it-works">
    <h2 id="how-it-works" class="type-heading-1 section-heading">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <div class="steps__body">
        <p><span class="step-title">Analyze any US-listed ticker.</span> Type a ticker or ask in plain words. From licensed market and options data, TwiceOver synthesizes the key technical levels, the macro backdrop and market regime, peer positioning, and fundamentals into one read — on any US-listed ticker, no broker connection required. Curated voices and the news wire are part of Core.</p>
        {/* The chart step 1's own copy already promises ("the key technical levels") — this is the one
            place on the page where a sentence named the artifact and the artifact was absent (#2992,
            site-prelaunch.md v2.31 §2). The paragraph above is a PM/Growth copy slot (site-copy-
            twiceover.md, final via #41) and ships VERBATIM — it is deliberately untouched.

            NO CAPTION YET. v2.31 specifies one beneath the chart ("Every level named, valued, and
            dated — from the data pipeline, not the model.") and marks it new copy PENDING A GROWTH
            REVIEW. The issue is explicit that the chart is not blocked on it but the caption is, so
            the slot ships empty rather than shipping unreviewed copy. Tracked on #2992. */}
        <div class="steps__chart"><TechnicalsPriceChart /></div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <p><span class="step-title">Connect read-only to make it yours</span> <span class="optional">(optional)</span>. Link your brokerage <strong>read-only</strong> and the same read runs on the positions you actually hold, measured against <strong>your own rules</strong>. TwiceOver can never place, change, or cancel an order, and never touches your funds.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  {/* Connect section (new, #2208, realizes #2190) — answers "will it work with my
      broker?" and "how much work is this?", the two questions that stall a signup
      and that nothing above this point on the page addresses. Placed here, not
      after Two doors: the heading needs How-it-works step 2 ("Connect read-only to
      make it yours") as its antecedent, and escalates into the Trust plate's
      structural guarantees directly below. Never after Two doors — that section's
      "neither door is visually promoted" invariant (site-prelaunch.md §2) would be
      broken by giving the deep door alone a dedicated follow-on section. Copy:
      Growth, consult 0672 (site-copy-twiceover.md "Connect section", Option 1) —
      supersedes the PM-verified #2190 three-step copy per two founder rejections
      of that structure in Designer review. */}
  <section class="connect" aria-labelledby="connect-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="connect-heading" class="connect__head">Same broker. Nothing new.</h2>
      <p class="connect__body">Interactive Brokers, Schwab, Fidelity, Robinhood, E*Trade, tastytrade, Webull, Vanguard and more — read-only, with <strong>the login you already have</strong>. TwiceOver can never place, change, or cancel an order, and never touches your funds.</p>
      <p class="connect__disclosure type-caption">Connections run through SnapTrade (SOC 2 Type II) and are authorized by your broker — credentials are entered there, never with TwiceOver.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Trust plate (v2.3, new — the one deliberate register break, dark-variant Ledger
      tokens, ADR 0035, scoped via [data-theme="dark"] to this section only). */}
  <section class="trust-plate" data-theme="dark" aria-labelledby="trust-plate">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="trust-plate" class="type-heading-1 section-heading">Built the honest way</h2>
      <div class="trust-grid">
        <div class="trust-card">
          <svg class="trust-card__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="11" width="12" height="9" rx="1.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M8 11V8a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg>
          <h3 class="type-heading-2">Read-only, structurally</h3>
          <p>Your brokerage connection can view your positions. It is technically incapable of placing, changing, or canceling an order.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="trust-card">
          <svg class="trust-card__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="4" width="14" height="17" rx="1.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M8 9h8M8 13h8M8 17h5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg>
          <h3 class="type-heading-2">Licensed data only</h3>
          <p>Every quote and news item comes from a licensed vendor — never scraped.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="trust-card">
          <svg class="trust-card__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l7 3v6c0 5-3 8-7 9-4-1-7-4-7-9V6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg>
          <h3 class="type-heading-2">Your book stays yours</h3>
          <p>Your account data and its analysis are never exposed to, cached for, or reused by another user.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="trust-card">
          <svg class="trust-card__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg>
          <h3 class="type-heading-2">Every number stamped</h3>
          <p>Every figure carries its source and the exact time it was fetched, so you always know how fresh it is.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* FAQ (v2.3, new; grouped v2.21 #2534; chevron #2532) — native
      details/summary accordion, no JS. Eleven items split into two labeled
      groups (site-prelaunch.md §FAQ v2.21) — mechanics unchanged: border.strong
      rules between every item, only the very first item of the whole list
      starts open. */}
  <section class="faq section-ground section-ground--lifted" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <div class="faq__intro">
      <p class="type-caption faq__kicker">FAQ</p>
      <h2 id="faq-heading" class="type-heading-1">Questions, answered plainly</h2>
      <p>The same plain-language answers we'd give if you asked us directly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq__list">
      <h3 class="type-caption faq__group-label">Before you sign up</h3>
      <details open>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">What is TwiceOver, exactly?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>A decision-support tool, not a registered investment adviser or broker-dealer. No recommendations, no trading signals, no scores, no ratings — and never a one-line verdict or a "buy" or "sell." It never executes trades and never holds your money — the decision stays with you.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">Can TwiceOver trade on my behalf?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>No. The brokerage connection is read-only, structurally — TwiceOver can view your positions but is technically incapable of placing, changing, or canceling an order, and it never touches your funds.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">Where does the data come from?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>Licensed market and news data — never scraped, and never dependent on a personal login shared between users.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">Do I need to connect my brokerage to use it?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>No. Every US-listed ticker gets the full read with no connection at all. Connecting read-only adds your own positions and your own rules to that same read — it's optional, always.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">Do I need a card to connect my brokerage?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>No. A free account can connect one brokerage read-only — no card and no trial required. Connecting doesn't change your monthly read count either: it's the same whether or not a broker is connected. A card is only needed to start a Core trial.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">What does a connected free account actually see?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>The same read as any tier, run on the positions you actually hold: your structure — net debit/credit, breakevens, max profit, max loss — your own configured rules evaluated on live data, and the paths available on what you hold. Curated voices and the licensed news wire are part of Core.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">Do I need to create an account to use it?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>No — that's a separate optional step, not a requirement. Every US-listed ticker gets the full read with no account, same as no connection. An account is only for saving your own rules, connecting your brokerage read-only, or subscribing to a paid plan.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">Is my account data shared with anyone?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>No. Your account data and its analysis are never exposed to, cached for, or reused by another user.</p>
      </details>
      <h3 class="type-caption faq__group-label">Once you're in</h3>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">What happens when the 14-day trial ends?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>Your saved card is charged $49/month, plus any applicable sales tax, and Core continues uninterrupted. We email you before that happens, and the app carries the date the whole time the trial is running. Cancelling before then is one click in Settings — no charge, and the account moves to Free with your rules, broker connection, and read history kept.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">How do I cancel?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>One click in Settings — no retention flow, no call, no form to fill in. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the period already paid for: Core stays on until that date, then the account moves to Free, keeping your rules, broker connection, and read history. Refunds are a separate matter, handled by Dodo Payments, our merchant of record — see the <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">What if connecting my brokerage fails?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>Nothing is connected and nothing is synced — a failed attempt leaves the account exactly as it was. The screen says so and offers Try again, which opens a fresh SnapTrade session where you can pick the same broker or a different one. Credentials are entered at SnapTrade, never with TwiceOver, so a failed attempt leaves nothing with us either.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">What if some of the data isn't available?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>The read says so, in the section where the gap is. A layer that couldn't be sourced is marked missing rather than filled in — nothing is estimated to paper over it, and no section is quietly dropped. A stated limitation is the honest result; a confident answer built on absent data is not.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="type-heading-2">How do I get support?<svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></summary>
        <p>There's one address: support@twiceover.io. It reaches a person rather than a queue, and we typically respond within 1–2 business days. It's the same address on the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.</p>
